<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Dogs mate (Continued), Mlie.DogsMate, Workshop 2441132298.

  What it reads: Defs/CompatibleSpecies/Canidae.xml declares the Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef "Dog",
  whose <pawnKinds> are Husky, LabradorRetriever and YorkshireTerrier. The mod only activates the crossings
  between kinds that share a group. Its own compatibility patches for other dog mods (for example
  Patches/akairo.ShibaWanko.xml) append their kinds to that same list, which is what this file does.

  Why the dalmatian goes in "Dog": it is a domestic dog in this mod, with vanilla's husky as its analogue
  (same body, same trade tags, same Advanced training), and the husky is in that group.

  Guard: a PatchOperationConditional on the group def. Without Dogs mate the xpath selects nothing, no
  <nomatch> is declared, and the operation reports success without logging. Not MayRequire: nothing reads
  it on an <Operation> (see ADSPatch.xml). No load order is needed, patches run once every def is loaded.

  Only the canonical CCPDalmatian is listed. WD_Dalmatian belongs to WhaleysDogs and is left alone.
-->
<Patch>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>Defs/Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef[defName="Dog"]/pawnKinds</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>Defs/Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef[defName="Dog"]/pawnKinds</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>CCPDalmatian</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
